# Render (and any host that sets NODE_ENV=production) makes `npm install`
# omit devDependencies. Since the Sep 2026 dependency audit, vite, esbuild and
# typescript live there — correctly, because the built server does not need
# them at runtime — but the BUILD does, so the deploy died on `vite: not found`.
#
# `include=dev` beats the omit that NODE_ENV implies, so the build gets its
# tooling back without moving build-only packages into runtime dependencies.
# The dev-only `await import("vite")` in server.ts stays behind its
# NODE_ENV !== "production" guard and is never reached in a deployed process.
include=dev
